{
  "id": 506003495,
  "iid": 25739,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "HTTP2: close-delimiter with CRLF or not",
  "description": "This change will enhance the heuristic check for multipart/mixed data.  The current behaviour assumes that there would be four bytes found after the boundary, consisting of \"--\\r\\n\".  This change also permits where the boundary is simply followed by the \"--\" delimiter.\n\nThis discrepancy was noted during 5G SA core testing where one vendor included the trailing \"\\r\\n\" and the packets where decoded, while another vendor does not include the \"\\r\\n\".  According to RFC2046, it does not appear that a CRLF is mandatory at the end of the multipart-body.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
